<Item XName="Note" UserName="Note" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;P class=MsoTitle style=&quot;BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 0.75pt solid; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; PADDING-TOP: 0in; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=6 face=Arial&gt;Parameterized Fast Circuit Envelope (FCE) &lt;BR&gt;simulation of an&amp;nbsp;LNA&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue Example Workspace&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;This example demonstrates use of a parameterized FCE file. Parameterized FCE files store FCE models for the same circuit extracted under different conditions (e.g. bias voltages, load resistances, temperatures).&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;The parameterized FCE file used in this example (L1_2var.fce) is for an LNA.&amp;nbsp;Models have been extracted for varying drain supply voltages (VDD) and load resistances (ROUT). The ranges over which these were varied can be seen in the custom GUI of the FastCircuitEnvelope model:&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=4 face=Arial&gt;VDD range is 3 - 5&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=4 face=Arial&gt;ROUT range is 30 - 100&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;The LN&lt;!--__SearchResult__0--&gt;&lt;/A&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;A FCE model has one input (QPSKPS1) and three outputs:&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=4 face=Arial&gt;CDC: current consumption (freq of interest is 0, i.e. DC)&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=4 face=Arial&gt;Pin: voltage at the real input of the LNA (freq of interest is 1.96GHz)&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=4 face=Arial&gt;Pout: output voltage of the LNA (freq of interest is 1.96GHz)&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;In &lt;EM&gt;Design1&lt;/EM&gt; the FastCircuitEnvelope model has been configured to only use the CDC and Pout outputs. A QPSK signal with symbol rate of 1 MHz modulating a 1.96 GHz carrier is applied to the input of the FastCircuitEnvelope model. The signal at the &lt;EM&gt;CDC&lt;/EM&gt; output is recorded in the Sink CDC and plotted in the Graph &lt;EM&gt;DC Current Consumption&lt;/EM&gt;. The spectrum and EVM of the signal at the &lt;EM&gt;Pout&lt;/EM&gt; output is measured and the results are shown in the Graph &lt;EM&gt;Output Spectrum and EVM&lt;/EM&gt;.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;Run the simulation for different values of VDD and ROUT and observe how the DC current consumption, output spectrum and EVM change.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;</Text>
<Item XName="Page" Type="PageMgr">
<Item XName="Display0" Type="NotesDisp">
<DVport><T>Array_Dbl64</T><D>1;4;;;i324;Cv14</D></DVport>
